<title>RUSSIA: Reuters 7th ex-Moscow air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 7th ex-Moscow air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-Moscow air cargo market rates in U.S. dollars per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>These rates exclude any cargo fuel surcharges, which are being applied by foreign airlines.</p>
<p>						 Nov 19    Oct 18</p>
<p>						 EUROPE</p>
<p>    SVO (Moscow-Sheremetyevo)-FRA    1.08	1.07</p>
<p>    SVO-LON				  1.15	1.15</p>
<p>    SVO-LUX				  1.31	1.30</p>
<p>		 ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p>    SVO-BKK				  3.30	3.30</p>
<p>    SVO-SEL				  4.02	4.05</p>
<p>    SVO-NRT				  4.19	4.20</p>
<p>		  MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>    SVO-DXB				  2.03	2.03</p>
<p>    SVO-SHJ				  2.40	2.40</p>
<p>		 UNITED STATES</p>
<p>    SVO-MIA				  3.34	3.35</p>
<p>    SVO-NYC				  2.62	2.63</p>
<p>    SVO-SFO				  3.22	3.24</p>
<p>The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at Moscow's Sheremetyevo international airport.</p>
<p>All prices are quoted in U.S. dollars</p>
<p>The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
